==Notes==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*Taking levels in this class does not increase [[spell slot]]s like taking levels in the [[pale master]] class would.
*This class is occasionally banned from some servers as the [[ability]] increases from dragon abilities are considered "overpowered".
* The extra [[skill point]] from increased intelligence starts when intelligence is increased at red dragon disciple level 9 (possibly as early as character level 14, which would result in 27 extra skill points by character level 40).

=== Previous versions ===

* Prior to the ''[[Enhanced Edition]]'' soft-coding the ability increases for this class, losing a red dragon disciple level that grants an ability bonus could leave a character with corrupted ability scores. This could be corrected by a [[Dungeon Master]] (DM), but not through [[script]]ing. For this reason, some servers that allow re-leveling without DM assistance banned this class.
** Soft-coding the ability increases had the side-effect of failing to give extra hit points from constitution increases (at class level 7).<ref>[https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/nwnecbguild/nwn-ee-rdd-7-and-retroactive-hp-gain-no-longer-occ-t2355523.html#p21402 NWN EE, RDD 7 and Retroactive HP gain no longer occurs?] @ Epic Character Builders Guild</ref> This lasted until a save-reload or logout-login. This has since been fixed.<!-- Version number? -->

== Custom content notes ==

* The trigger for getting wings consists of having the ''dragon abilities'' feat and then taking a ninth level in this class. This aspect is hardcoded to both the feat and the class, with the feat check apparently happening before the level-up is applied.

